@* The index-data pane's row of PER-DOCUMENT actions — things the user does to the document they picked, as
   opposed to things they do to the form (ADR 0550 keeps Save/Cancel out of here, with the fields they commit).

   Extracted from the workbench shell (ADR 0558's direction, forced by the shell's size ratchet when Compare
   versions moved up here — ADR 0664). It renders inside IndexDataPane's <ReadActions> fragment, which the shell
   supplies, so the shell still decides that this row exists; it no longer has to hold its markup.

   IT INJECTS NOTHING, AND THAT IS LOAD-BEARING. The first version of this component read DetailState and
   DetailEditor directly, like the pane it sits in — and froze. Its only parameters were six EventCallbacks
   built from METHOD GROUPS, which C# caches, so every parent render handed it byte-identical parameter values;
   Blazor's diff concluded nothing could have changed and skipped re-rendering it. The row therefore showed
   whatever was true at first paint and never updated, so the share and compare buttons — the two whose
   conditions are only satisfied once the shell's async load finishes — were simply absent, on a document that
   had both. It corrected itself on a tab switch, because that re-creates the tree structurally.

   So the state arrives as PARAMETERS: a value that changes is a parameter that changes, and the component
   re-renders because Blazor can see that it must. It also makes the row honest — it renders what it is given
   and knows nothing about where the answers came from.

   ONE VOCABULARY (ADR 0511): every entry is an icon with a tooltip, always visible rather than revealed on
   hover, because touch has no hover. The tooltip IS the label here, so each button needs its OWN MudTooltip
   wrapping it — nesting one button inside another's tooltip makes it wear that neighbour's text, which is
   exactly what the chain icon did until ADR 0664. *@

@* Follow / unfollow this document (ADR "Document subscriptions"). *@
<MudTooltip Text="@(Subscribed ? Strings.Get("UnfollowDoc") : Strings.Get("FollowDoc"))">
    <MudIconButton Size="Size.Small" aria-label="Follow"
                   Icon="@(Subscribed ? Icons.Material.Filled.Notifications : Icons.Material.Outlined.NotificationsNone)"
                   Color="@(Subscribed ? Color.Primary : Color.Default)"
                   OnClick="@(() => Follow.InvokeAsync())" />
</MudTooltip>
@* Set a reminder (Wiedervorlage) on this document (ADR "Document reminders"). *@
<MudTooltip Text="@Strings.Get("RemindTooltip")">
    <MudIconButton Size="Size.Small" aria-label="Remind" Icon="@Icons.Material.Filled.Alarm"
                   OnClick="@(() => Remind.InvokeAsync())" />
</MudTooltip>
@* Share with someone who has no account (ADR 0546); an absent rel means it is not offered (ADR 0543). *@
@if (CanShare)
{
    <MudTooltip Text="@Strings.Get("ExtLinkManage")">
        <MudIconButton Size="Size.Small" aria-label="@Strings.Get("ExtLinkManage")"
                       Icon="@Icons.Material.Filled.Link" OnClick="@(() => Share.InvokeAsync())" />
    </MudTooltip>
}
@* Compare two versions (ADR 0664). It lived at the BOTTOM of the pane until it was found scrolled out of
   sight on an ordinary document, and moved here because it is a per-document action like its neighbours. *@
@if (VersionCount >= 2)
{
    <MudTooltip Text="@Strings.Get("CompareVersionsBtn")">
        <MudIconButton Size="Size.Small" aria-label="@Strings.Get("CompareVersionsBtn")"
                       Icon="@Icons.Material.Filled.Difference" OnClick="@(() => Compare.InvokeAsync())" />
    </MudTooltip>
}
@* Manage access (ACL) — only when the caller can manage permissions (ADR "Manage-access UI"). *@
@if (CanManagePermissions)
{
    <MudTooltip Text="@Strings.Get("MaManageAccess")">
        <MudIconButton data-tour="action-manage-access" Size="Size.Small" aria-label="Manage access"
                       Icon="@Icons.Material.Filled.Security" OnClick="@(() => ManageAccess.InvokeAsync())" />
    </MudTooltip>
}
@* Edit the index data (issue #407) — beside the thing it edits rather than at the far end of the pane. *@
@if (CanEdit)
{
    <MudTooltip Text="@Strings.Get("Edit")">
        <MudIconButton data-tour="action-edit-index" Size="Size.Small" aria-label="@Strings.Get("Edit")"
                       Icon="@Icons.Material.Filled.Edit" OnClick="@(() => Edit.InvokeAsync())" Disabled="Busy" />
    </MudTooltip>
}

@code {
    [Parameter] public bool Subscribed { get; set; }
    [Parameter] public bool CanShare { get; set; }
    [Parameter] public int VersionCount { get; set; }
    [Parameter] public bool CanManagePermissions { get; set; }
    [Parameter] public bool CanEdit { get; set; }
    [Parameter] public bool Busy { get; set; }

    [Parameter] public EventCallback Follow { get; set; }
    [Parameter] public EventCallback Remind { get; set; }
    [Parameter] public EventCallback Share { get; set; }
    [Parameter] public EventCallback Compare { get; set; }
    [Parameter] public EventCallback ManageAccess { get; set; }
    [Parameter] public EventCallback Edit { get; set; }
}
